    "field": "Climate change impacts on agriculture and ecosystems",
    "problem": "The development of effective climate adaptation policies for Central American smallholders is hindered because historical climate evidence is fragmentary and a decade of diverse modeling research on agricultural and ecological impacts has not been synthesized to provide clear guidance.",
    "method": "This paper reviews and synthesizes a decade of modeling research on agricultural and ecological climate change impacts in Central America to identify expected impacts, key research gaps, and policy actions to minimize them.",
    "task": "The task is to review a decade of research modeling the impacts of climate change on smallholder agriculture and ecosystems in Central America to synthesize expected changes and guide future adaptation responses.",
